    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p39-q34-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{x}{x+1}+\\frac2{x-2}=1.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-4$.",
          "worked": "$x\\ne-1,2$. Multiply by $(x+1)(x-2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x-2)+2(x+1)&=(x+1)(x-2)\\\\x^2+2&=x^2-x-2\\\\x+4&=0\\\\x&=-4.\\end{align*}$$\nThis value is admissible.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q35-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{2x}{x-3}-\\frac{x+1}{x+2}=1.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac97$.",
          "worked": "$x\\ne3,-2$. Multiply by $(x-3)(x+2)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x(x+2)-(x+1)(x-3)&=(x-3)(x+2)\\\\x^2+6x+3&=x^2-x-6\\\\7x+9&=0\\\\x&=-\\frac97.\\end{align*}$$\nThis value is admissible.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q36-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{3x}{x+4}+\\frac{x-2}{x-1}=2.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$ or $x=\\frac72$.",
          "worked": "$x\\ne-4,1$. Multiply by $(x+4)(x-1)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x(x-1)+(x-2)(x+4)&=2(x+4)(x-1)\\\\4x^2-x-8&=2x^2+6x-8\\\\2x^2-7x&=0\\\\x(2x-7)&=0\\\\x&=0\\text{ or }x=\\frac72.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are admissible.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q37-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{x+2}{x-1}-\\frac{x}{x+1}=2.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1\\pm\\sqrt2$.",
          "worked": "$x\\ne\\pm1$. Multiply by $(x-1)(x+1)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+2)(x+1)-x(x-1)&=2(x-1)(x+1)\\\\4x+2&=2x^2-2\\\\x^2-2x-1&=0\\\\(x-1)^2&=2\\\\x-1&=\\pm\\sqrt2\\\\x&=1\\pm\\sqrt2.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are admissible.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q38-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac4{x-2}-\\frac{x}{x+1}=-2.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0$ or $x=-4$.",
          "worked": "$x\\ne2,-1$. Multiply by $(x-2)(x+1)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}4(x+1)-x(x-2)&=-2(x-2)(x+1)\\\\-x^2+6x+4&=-2x^2+2x+4\\\\x^2+4x&=0\\\\x(x+4)&=0\\\\x&=0\\text{ or }x=-4.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values are admissible.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p39-q39-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$\\frac{x-1}{x+1}+\\frac{2x}{x-4}=1.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No real solution.",
          "worked": "$x\\ne-1,4$. Multiply by $(x+1)(x-4)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-1)(x-4)+2x(x+1)&=(x+1)(x-4)\\\\3x^2-3x+4&=x^2-3x-4\\\\2x^2+8&=0\\\\x^2&=-4.\\end{align*}$$\nA real square cannot be negative, so there is no real solution.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
  },
